<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wu Peifu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1874">1874</a>–<a href="/years/1939">1939</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wu Peifu was a Chinese general and leader of the Zhili clique, one of the strongest warlords of the 1920s. He defeated the Anhui clique in 1920 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhang-zuolin">Zhang Zuolin</a>'s Fengtian clique in 1922, but was betrayed by Feng Yuxiang in 1924. His armies were destroyed during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuomintang">Kuomintang</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-expedition">Northern Expedition</a> of 1926–1927.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wu-peifu.jpg" alt="Wu Peifu" width="320" height="462" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wu_Peifu_with_sword.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
